      "title": "Small farms pursue saffron, seed processing and direct vegetable sales",
      "content_html": "Four farm profiles from Poland and Romania show how producers earn income from agriculture. Dorota Kaliszewska, a Polish farmer in the Lublin region, is testing saffron; Romanian grower Robert Zamisnicu cultivates vegetables and melons on 40 hectares; and Polish pumpkin-seed entrepreneur Łukasz Popielewicz relies on contract growers and processing. Filip and Magda Partyka run a 14-hectare vegetable farm and sell directly to households.\n\nZamisnicu said an early-August hailstorm damaged about half his crop, while Kaliszewska lost some saffron bulbs to excess moisture in her first season. Popielewicz's company handled about 5,000 tonnes of pumpkin seeds last year and is targeting up to 9,000 tonnes this year, depending on the harvest.",
