      "id": "https://gizmodo.com/its-like-gta-musk-touts-video-game-like-update-to-tesla-fsd-2000843584",
      "url": "https://gizmodo.com/its-like-gta-musk-touts-video-game-like-update-to-tesla-fsd-2000843584",
      "title": "Tesla begins FSD v15 rollout with new driving display and safety claims",
      "content_html": "Tesla has begun sending its Full Self-Driving (Supervised) v15 software to early-access owners, adding a live, photorealistic visualization called Tesla Reality View and claiming a 25-fold improvement in handling safety-critical situations. The update also targets sign recognition, potholes, road debris, standing water and speed control near schools and in bad weather. Tesla says the supervised system can slow for detected speed cameras and adds a mode for cars carrying bike racks.\n\nReality View renders the surroundings from a virtual camera above the car and displays planned turns. Tesla says it lets drivers see and control what FSD intends to do. The company attributes the claimed safety improvement to an upgraded vision encoder trained on millions of internet videos, but has not published the underlying intervention rate, making the multiplier difficult to assess independently. Tesla chief executive Elon Musk said the wider release is planned for December with Tesla’s 2026 Holiday Update. Tesla has not identified which vehicles will receive the first general-release builds.",
